%S A400754 1,7,43,268,1708,11005,71170,460681,2982355,19306753,124982332,
%T A400754 809064574,5237405107,33903830536,219473110969,1420737623107,
%U A400754 9197005659379,59535914766064,385399910681296,2494848560932465,16150157719613386,104546463639352297,676771289109138103
%N A400754 Row sums of the Riordan array (1/(1-3*x)^2, x/(1-3*x)^3).
%C A400754 a(n) is the number of objects of size n consisting of two initial words followed by a sequence of blocks, where each block is a marker of size 1 followed by three words. Words are possibly empty and are over a 3-letter alphabet; the size of a word is its length.
%C A400754 The Riordan array (1/(1-3*x)^2, x/(1-3*x)^3) = (u'(x), u(x)*u'(x)), where u(x) = x/(1-3*x), is the derivative array associated with u, in the sense of Bang et al. See also A400753.
%H A400754 Caroline Bang, Matias von Bell, Eric Culver, Jessica Dickson, Stoyan Dimitrov, Rachel Perrier, and Sheila Sundaram, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL26/Bell/vonbell6.html">On sums, derivatives, and flips of Riordan arrays</a>, J. Integer Seq., Vol. 26 (2023), Article 23.2.7.
%H A400754 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (10,-27,27).
%F A400754 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} binomial(n+2*k+1, 3*k+1)*3^(n-k).
%F A400754 G.f.: (1-3*x)/(1-10*x+27*x^2-27*x^3).
%F A400754 a(n) = 10*a(n-1) - 27*a(n-2) + 27*a(n-3) for n >= 3, with a(0)=1, a(1)=7, a(2)=43.
%F A400754 a(n) = Sum_{r=0..n} 3^(n-r)*A400753(r).
%t A400754 LinearRecurrence[{10, -27, 27}, {1, 7, 43}, 23]
%Y A400754 Cf. A124820 and A192810 (analogous row sums with 3 replaced by 1 and 2), A400753.
%K A400754 nonn,easy,new
%O A400754 0,2
%A A400754 _Ifeyinwa Madu_, Oct 05 2026
